  "text": "I built a 6-second, 30 fps ambient loop at 1920×1080 on a deep indigo background. The contact sheet shows it rendering, and frame 5.97s lines up with frame 0 (the closing frame is one frame before the loop point).\n\n- **Orbs:** Five blurred, soft-edged orbs (**Orb Purple**, **Orb Teal**, **Orb Violet**, **Orb Cyan**, **Orb Indigo**) drift slowly in small elliptical paths. I drove them with sine and cosine expressions that each complete a whole number of cycles in exactly 6 seconds, so there are no keyframes or seam to ease around.\n- **Dot grid:** A 16×9 grid of small white dots, built as nine row layers. Each row's opacity pulses gently between about 8% and 36%. Each row is offset slightly from the one above, so the pulse ripples down the screen. It also loops cleanly at 6 seconds.\n\nI didn't run critique. The dots are very faint in the thumbnails, so if the stage screen is washed out, raise the 22 and 14 in the row opacity expressions.\n\nNext I could make the orbs larger and slower for a calmer feel, or change the palette toward the conference's brand colors.",
